course: dictionary
lesson: 7868
title: Taking words apart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are two smaller words joined together. These are called compound words, and you can often work out their meaning from their parts. Raindrop is made of rain and drop. Rain is water falling from clouds, and a drop is a small round bit of liquid, so a raindrop is one small drop of water from the rain.
explain: Look at the words around it too. «Raindrops on the window» tells you where raindrops can be: on the glass, running down it. «The first raindrops» means the first drops to fall when a shower begins.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Small raindrops are round, and bigger ones are flattened at the bottom like a burger bun as they fall.» If a raindrop is one small drop of water, the sentence makes sense: a drop of water is round, and it changes shape as it falls.
fact: A raindrop is a single small drop of water that falls from a cloud as rain.
fact: Raindrop is a compound word: rain plus drop.
fact: In the water cycle, tiny droplets in clouds join together until they are heavy enough to fall as rain.
fact: Sunlight passing through raindrops makes a rainbow.
fact: «Small raindrops are round, and bigger ones are flattened at the bottom like a burger bun.» None is shaped like a teardrop.
exercise: What is a raindrop? | A flat puddle on the ground | *A single small drop of water that falls from a cloud as rain | A large cloud full of water | A drop of paint on a window
exercise: In «raindrops on the window», where are the raindrops? | Far out at sea | *On the glass | Inside a bottle | Under the bed
exercise: Which two smaller words make up raindrop? | rain and bow | ran and drop | rain and drip | *rain and drop
test: «Some cars have a rain sensor that switches the wipers on when raindrops change the reflection.» What switches the wipers on? | The sun shining on the car | A driver pressing a button | *Raindrops changing the reflection of light | Dust on the windscreen
test: In a cloud, what happens before a raindrop falls? | *Tiny droplets join together until they are heavy enough to fall | Sunlight melts the drop | The cloud turns into a rock | The water rises from the ground into the sky
exam: «In cold clouds, raindrops usually start as ice.» Where do raindrops in cold clouds usually start? | As warm steam from the sea | As dust on the ground | *As ice crystals | As a rainbow in the sky
